{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3430","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3430","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3430\",\"parent_revision\":\"876fd57bb148e0290ca8d28f14a4b1f7b061896b1966d6a1d1e81ff457e728ed\",\"root_revision\":\"876fd57bb148e0290ca8d28f14a4b1f7b061896b1966d6a1d1e81ff457e728ed\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Chore\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-09-06\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n`rules/skill-substitution.md` documents `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}` and `${CLAUDE_SKILL_DIR}` as substituting throughout a rendered SKILL.md body, and states explicitly that `references/*.md` are not substituted. It says nothing about agent bodies.\\n\\nImpact if this stands: nobody can safely reference a plugin-root file from an agent. An author either avoids the variable and duplicates content into every agent, or uses it and ships an agent that reads a literal `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}` string and cannot find the file. Both failures are silent.\\n\\nEVIDENCE GATHERED, INCONCLUSIVE. Across the repo only one pre-existing agent uses the variable: `plugins/summarizer/agents/file-summarizer.md:24` runs `$CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT/scripts/file_metrics.py` inside a Bash command. That is the real process env var supplied to hooks and commands \u2014 a separate mechanism from load-time text substitution \u2014 so it is not evidence either way. Six further uses in `plugins/plugin-creator/agents/` were added in this session and then removed for exactly this reason.\\n\\nCURRENT WORKAROUND: those six agents state the three-part portability test inline with no path. Correct and safe, since inlining is one of the three placements the rule itself allows, but it duplicates a sentence that a pointer would carry once.\\n\\nTEST: use the canary procedure `rules/skill-substitution.md` names \u2014 `/example-argument-substitution`. Put a `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}` reference and a no-variable control line in an agent body, dispatch that agent, and observe whether the variable arrives expanded or literal. The control line distinguishes substitution from the agent inferring the path from context.\\n\\nTHEN, whichever way it lands:\\n- Record the answer in `rules/skill-substitution.md`, which currently scopes its claim to SKILL.md and leaves agents undefined.\\n- If agents DO substitute: the six plugin-creator agents can point at `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/docs/runtime-environment.md` instead of restating the test, removing the duplication.\\n- If agents do NOT substitute: state that explicitly in the rule, so the next author reaches for inlining or a skill activation rather than discovering it by shipping a broken agent.\\n\\nRelated: #3429 covers the separate skilllint LK001 workaround affecting SKILL.md link syntax. Do not conflate \u2014 that one is an upstream tooling bug, this one is an unverified platform behaviour.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session melodic-plotting-emerson (2026-09-06), PR #3427\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-09-06\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"9a64e69a8292d7352ad816e2dab32445d960fdb89c97fb02f709ab4ed6d4cfa6\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABSzTLXQ\"}"}